---

# THREE.JS USAGE

Use 3D sparingly.

Not for gimmicks.

Examples

Floating Portal

Constellation Sphere

Animated Planet

Sacred Geometry

Energy Crystal

Astral Compass

Light Rings

Particle Systems

Depth Backgrounds

Avoid heavy GPU usage.

Everything should remain elegant.

---

# DESIGN LANGUAGE

Think less

Apple Dashboard

Think more

A24 Movie

Dune

Arrival

Interstellar

Journey

The Fountain

Blade Runner 2049 (spiritual version)

Studio Ghibli dreamscapes

The UI should feel like cinematic production design.

---

# NAVIGATION

Navigation should never dominate.

Menus may

Fade

Materialize

Hide

Float

Appear only when needed

Icons can become constellations.

Navigation itself should become part of the world.

---

# PLACEHOLDER STRATEGY

Do NOT use photographs.

Do NOT use stock images.

Do NOT use random illustrations.

Instead create environments using

Abstract geometry

Light

Glass

Fog

Particles

Constellations

Floating gradients

Astral architecture

Decorative bands

Sacred circles

Volumetric lighting

Every placeholder should already feel like final art direction.

---

# FINAL CREATIVE DIRECTIVE

Forget modern SaaS.

Forget landing pages.

Forget dashboards.

Forget conventional UI.

Imagine that Frecuencia Mágica is the operating system of another universe.

Every interaction should make the user whisper:

> **"I've never seen a website like this before."**

> **"Prioritize memorability over familiarity. Break common web conventions whenever usability is preserved. The goal is not to look modern; the goal is to create an unforgettable digital experience that users will remember months later."**
